          "message": "[atom vllm]Fix Qwen3.5 block-FP8 correctness under vLLM FULL cudagraph (#1985)\n\n* Fix Qwen3.5 block-FP8 correctness under vLLM FULL cudagraph.\n\nRestore the 0526-compatible MHA path for Qwen3.5 only, fix GDN prefill/dispatch\nand metadata compaction on vLLM 0.27+, and scope MoE MORI trim so other models\nkeep the existing behavior.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Fix Pre Checkin lint and update GDN metadata tests.\n\nFormat mori_patch for Black, fix ruff import/order/SIM102/RUF012/BLE001\non PR-touched files, and align Kimi K3 tests with removal of GDN FULL-graph\nmetadata compaction.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Refactor Qwen3.5 MHA fix to plugin-only scope.\n\nMove legacy PagedAttention routing into qwen35_attention_patch via\nregister hook and revert core model_ops/qwen3_5 changes. Standalone\nATOM on main needs no core patch for this probe.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Scope Qwen3.5 MHA/MoE plugin patches to 35B-A3B only.\n\n397B CI regressed when the FULL-cudagraph MHA bridge applied to all Qwen3.5 variants; restrict it via config fingerprint while keeping the 35B customer fix.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: zhangxinyuanliuhengyu <zhangxinyuanliuhengyu@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: xinyuazh <xinyuazh@users.noreply.github.com>",
