          "id": "53a904ce35f92b2600fbd9be1b62dba62cddfbfb",
          "message": "style: clear the lint findings CI reports on this diff\n\nCI installs the latest ruff and runs it with no config, so its default\nrule set is wider than the local 0.15.14's (RUF059, UP045, C408, RUF007\nall fire there and none fire here). reviewdog reports with\n-filter-mode=diff_context, so only findings on this branch's lines fail\nthe check.\n\n  RUF059  two unpacked values that are genuinely unused -> _arange,\n          _prefill_positions. Kept as unpacking rather than indexing so\n          the tuple's shape stays visible at the call site.\n  UP045   Optional[X] -> X | None in ubatch_splitting.py. Converted all\n          ten, not just the six CI flagged: the other four are main's\n          lines, but leaving them would mix both spellings in one file\n          and keep an import alive for four annotations.\n  C408    dict(...) -> a literal in test_scheduler.py.\n  RUF007  zip(xs, xs[1:]) -> itertools.pairwise in test_tbo_mixed_split.\n\nVerified the way CI decides: every ruff finding cross-referenced against\nthe lines this branch touches plus three lines of context. Zero remain.\nThe 36 E402/E731 that survive are pre-existing -- identical count with\nand without these commits.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
