          "id": "9db8e0770f5fa53bcdb43113b47a41580287cc4c",
          "message": "ci(benchmark): give an agentic cell enough wall clock to finish\n\n`timeout-minutes: 80` killed the c=48 cell 3.5 minutes from the end. The\nreplay is only part of the wall clock: on that cell, dataset configuration\nplus the warmup that primes every lane's prefix cache took 23.5 min before\nprofiling even started (11:04:47 step start -> 11:28:21 profiling -> due\n12:28:21, killed 12:24:47), and warmup scales with the lane count, so the\nhigher-concurrency cells were never going to fit either. Three of five cells\ndied this way and produced no result at all.\n\nRaise the step to 180 min for agentic runs only; random keeps 80.\n\nAlso fix the ordering of the two limits, which mattered as much as the number.\n`atom_test.sh`'s drain supervisor was `duration/60 + 60` = 120 min, under the\nstep timeout by a margin that the observed 87-minute cell would have eaten. Set\nit to `duration/60 + 90` = 150 and keep the step strictly above it, so an\noverrun is killed by the supervisor -- which logs why and lets the step\ncontinue to the artifact upload -- rather than by the runner, which takes the\nwhole step down and loses `profile_export.jsonl` with it. That file is the only\nsource for the p90 e2e normalized interactivity the dashboard publishes; it\ncannot be rebuilt from the aggregate columns.\n\nSigned-off-by: ZhangLirong-amd <Lirong.Zhang@amd.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-08-27T12:47:20Z",
