          "id": "4a02b0f7aed5471002aff1ff822efa23dffc3668",
          "message": "fake-eplb: route on a zero router correction bias (#2010)\n\n* fake-eplb: route on a zero router correction bias\n\nThe noaux_tc correction bias is added on top of the score before top-k, so\na bias wider than the synthetic logits' post-score gap (~3.16 after\nsqrtsoftplus, 1.0 after sigmoid) decides the selection on its own. Under\n`--load_dummy` the bias is never written, so it holds whatever the recycled\nallocation left behind -- observed up to 7.5e3 on DeepSeek-V4-Flash, which\nsent 100% of the tokens to EP rank 0 on every DP rank.\n\nVerified on V4-Flash-FP8, dp4 + EP + --load_dummy + --fake-eplb: per-rank\ntop-k goes from rankhist=[98304,0,0,0] to an exactly uniform [98304]*4\naggregated over the four DP ranks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Apply the simulated-DP repeat to the MoE token capacity at dp_size == 1\n\n#2006 sizes the AITER topK buffer for the DP-attention gather, but gates the\nwhole adjustment on dp_size > 1. `repeat_rows` -- which stands in for the DP\nranks a simulated run did not launch -- also runs in `forward_impl`, the\nsingle-real-rank path, where it multiplies the rows on its own with no gather\nto ride along with. A `--fake-eplb` run simulating a wide deployment on one\nvisible device (e.g. -tp 8 --enable-dp-attention on 1 GPU, dp_logical_ratio=8)\ntherefore still undersizes the buffer and trips\n`assert total_topk_weights.shape[0] >= tokens_num` in select_experts.\n\nApply the repeat factor when dp_size == 1 as well. All2all/EP keeps tokens\nlocal and is unchanged; the gathered case keeps dp_size * repeat exactly as\n#2006 computes it.\n\nChecked against six configurations (all2all, gather, simulated with 2 real\nranks, simulated on 1 device, no simulation, pure DP): only the\nsingle-device simulated case changes, 16384 -> 131072.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
