          "message": "perf(v4): build the decode indptrs on the device, and bound compress per token (#2101)\n\nThe three ragged indptr cumsums (SWA/CSA/HCA) and the CSA per-token visibility\nwere rebuilt on the host every decode step: three numpy cumsums plus four H2D\ncopies of arrays whose every input already lived on the device.\n`build_v4_paged_decode_indptr` replaces that with one Triton launch reading\n`batch_id_per_token` and `positions` where they already are, so the four staging\nbuffers lose their host mirrors along with it.\n\nThe same build drops the per-SEQUENCE compress bound `ctx // ratio` for the\nper-TOKEN causal one, `(pos + 1) // ratio`, everywhere it appeared -- ATOM decode\nand prefill, both plugin bridges, and the two kernels in `deepseek_v4_ops`.\n`ctx // ratio` is the LAST token's count, and an MTP or DSpark sequence hands\n`1 + k` tokens to one forward, so giving it to the earlier ones lets them read\ncompressed groups holding their own future drafts. It was never a second cap\neither: it cannot bind while `pos < ctx`, which `require_step_within_full_q` now\nchecks at ATOM's three producers of per-seq step lengths instead of leaving\nassumed. `n_committed_hca_per_seq` disappears with its last reader; the CSA twin\nsurvives for the two uses that are genuinely per-sequence, the indexer's\n`cu_committed` cumsum and the FP4 ragged windows.\n\n`visible_csa` / `visible_hca` in `v4_pool_geometry` are the one home for the\nrule. The twenty host-side sites that used to spell it inline call them instead,\nwhich is what keeps the axis from drifting again; the Triton kernels take the\nratio as a `constexpr` and divide inline, and the reference implementations stay\nhand-written so they can still fail a kernel that restates the rule wrongly.\n\nGuards on a buffer bound raise `ValueError` rather than assert, since a\ntruncated `[:n]` slice is a device-side out-of-bounds write and `python -O`\nstrips asserts.\n\nTests: `test_decode_indptr_build` pins kernel against reference and both against\na written-out answer; `test_decode_indptr_qlen_invariance` pins a token's counts\nacross steps of differing query length; `test_v4_compress_visibility_lemma`\nenumerates, on the CPU so CI runs it, why the dropped bound could never bind.",
