          "distinct": true,
          "id": "e7212d177fc22c0b6ae8ea9cad31c780925aecf3",
          "message": "fix(loader): zero packed fp4x2 dummy weights via byte-view fallback (#2098)\n\ninitialize_dummy_weights(mode=\"zero\") called data.zero_() on every param,\nbut packed sub-byte dtypes (Float4_e2m1fn_x2) have no CUDA fill kernel, so\nzero_() raises RuntimeError ('\"fill_cuda\" not implemented for ...'). This\ncrashed --load_dummy=zero on MXFP4 checkpoints.\n\nKeep data.zero_() as the fast path (valid for all shapes and standard\ndtypes) and fall back to zeroing the raw bytes (data.view(torch.uint8)\n.zero_()) when it raises. All-zero bytes == zero-valued weights, and only\npacked weights (contiguous, >=1D) reach the fallback, so the uint8 view is\nalways valid there. Catch both RuntimeError (ATen dtype-dispatch miss) and\nNotImplementedError (backend-dispatch miss) to be robust across the two\nways PyTorch surfaces a missing fill kernel.\n\nAdds a regression test that forces the fallback (primary zero_() raises)\nand asserts the bytes end up zeroed.\n\nCo-authored-by: sim builder <sim-builder@atom.local>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-09-01T13:08:02+08:00",
          "tree_id": "ba42c842b964b35a228450fd749967885c4c66f1",
          "url": "https://github.com/ROCm/ATOM/commit/e7212d177fc22c0b6ae8ea9cad31c780925aecf3"
