          "id": "9c4db67e64604cadf09ba323fb5a9455478e9c01",
          "message": "ci(benchmark): bound agentic DP TTFT with a 20s prefill-delayer queue cap\n\nThe delayer coalesces prefills against a fill target, which leaves worst-case\nTTFT unbounded: a request can sit in the waiting queue as long as the target\nkeeps failing to be met. ATOM_PREFILL_DELAYER_MAX_QUEUE_MS force-releases once\nany rank's oldest schedulable waiting prefill has queued that long, so the tail\nhas a ceiling.\n\n20s is a backstop, not an operating point. The env's own note warns that a\nsmall value under heavy backlog fires every tick and defeats coalescing, so\nthis is sized well above the fill target: it should never fire on a healthy\nrun, and when it does it caps the tail rather than reshaping the schedule.\n\nPinned in the DP-only env set alongside the other delayer vars, which the\ncatalog test asserts in both directions -- the DPA variant carries all of them,\nthe TP variant none.",
