          "message": "ci: drop the Meta-Llama-3-8B-Instruct accuracy test (#2135)\n\nThe Meta-Llama-3-8B-Instruct entry is removed from the accuracy matrix. It has\nbeen failing on main on every recent run, and the model is no longer part of\nwhat ATOM needs to track. The pull-request accuracy set goes from 14 models to\n13; nightly goes from 41 to 40.\n\nTwo things referenced that entry and are updated with it.\n\nThe atomesh standalone whitelist in atomesh-accuracy-validation.yaml listed\nMeta-Llama-3-8B-Instruct as its only \"pr\" model. It filters against\nmodels_accuracy.json, so with the entry gone the key would have matched nothing\nwhile still reading as intentional. The key is removed and the consequence is\nwritten down: atomesh standalone now validates zero models on a pull request.\nPromoting a replacement changes what every atomesh PR pays for in runner time,\nso that is left to the job owner rather than decided here.\n\nThe offline inference smoke test in atom-test.yaml is deliberately left alone.\nIt uses the same model but is not an accuracy test: it asserts that the offline\nentrypoint completes, guarding the path the nightly Docker release smoke-tests,\nand its own comment records a hang that reached main and surfaced a day later.\nIts SMOKE_EXTRA_ARGS comment pointed at the accuracy entry, so the comment is\nrewritten to stand on its own. docker-release.yaml's golden-output check also\nstill uses this model and is unchanged for the same reason.",
          "timestamp": "2026-09-04T02:52:29Z",
