          "distinct": true,
          "id": "bba3c19371ac34b55f2f3fe0706f70b70e003c8a",
          "message": "[ATOMesh] Fix Spur scheduling, network setup, and benchmark outcomes (#2270)\n\n* Fix LMCache disk path for Crusoe submit host\n\n* fix(atomesh): use Slurm defaults for TW benchmark jobs\n\n* fix(atomesh): add amd-spur partition option\n\n* Fix Spur job monitoring and preserve jobs on status query failures\n\n* Fix namespaced model paths in ATOMesh benchmark configuration\n\n* Fix Ruff findings and format Slurm monitoring tests\n\n* Fix Spur batch dispatch for multi-node PD workers\n\n* Fix Kimi-K3 DSpark draft model paths under Inferact\n\n* Select NCCL socket interface from the Spur node address\n\n* Bind MORI bootstrap to the Spur node interface\n\n* Use ATOM host IP for Mooncake control traffic\n\n* Make ATOMesh RDMA GID indices configurable and default to IPv6 GID 0\n\n* Add amd-atom Slurm account and QoS to ATOMesh workflow\n\n* Configure ATOMesh node candidate pool and use -w for node selection\n\n* Fix Black formatting in ATOMesh node selection test\n\n* Fix Ruff findings in Slurm node selection tests\n\n* Restore IPv4 GID defaults and leave model Mooncake GID unset\n\n* Use completed ATOMesh workload results for Spur CI outcomes\n\n* Fix formatting and executable mode for ATOMesh result checks\n\n* Fix Mooncake matched-rail control addresses and listener test setup\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Junyan Yang <junyyang@crs-m2m-cpu-spur-v2-009.us-east2-a.compute.internal>\nCo-authored-by: junyan.yang@amd.com <junyan.yang@amd.com@pit2-vm-amd-xl-02.amd.pit2.tensorwave.lan>",
