          "distinct": true,
          "id": "af0f76017dcfe2dc719af6adb4ba72d9f596f44f",
          "message": "fix(release): model cache, dist/ ownership, stale release refs (#2304)\n\n* ci(release): serve the smoke model from the runner cache\n\nThe nightly release test pulled Meta-Llama-3-8B-Instruct from the hub on\nevery run, on both lines. On 2026-09-18 the rocm10.0 line died 11s in\nwhen huggingface.co dropped the connection under list_repo_templates.\n\nThat call is built to fall back to local files when the network is down,\nbut it catches httpx.NetworkError, and a mid-request disconnect raises\nRemoteProtocolError -- a sibling of NetworkError, not a subclass -- so it\nescaped and failed the build. Two seconds earlier the same process had\ncompleted a hub round-trip for config.json, which is what makes this a\ndropped connection rather than a broken image.\n\nMount the runner's model cache and pass a local directory, as\natom-test.yaml already does: transformers then takes its is_local branch\nand the failing call is never made. Move the download lock onto the\nshared mount, where the two lines can see each other's flock. On\nfailure, probe the hub from inside the container, so a dropped\nconnection and a broken image stop leaving the same trace in the log.\n\nVerified in atom_rocm10:ci against an endpoint that disconnects\nmid-request: list_repo_templates raises RemoteProtocolError and escapes,\nwhile a local path loads the tokenizer with networking disabled.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: retry a model download that fails in transport\n\nsnapshot_download ran once. A dropped connection on a cold cache, or on\nthe night an upstream revision changes, failed the job outright -- the\nsame class of event this script already survives during the revision\nlookup, where it falls back to the local cache.\n\nRetry with a linear backoff, resuming from what is already staged. Two\nfailures are not retried: a gated, missing, or unauthorized repo, which\nthe python side marks with exit 2 because every attempt reaches the same\nrefusal, and a timeout, which has already spent its budget.\n\nVerified in atom_rocm10:ci -- an endpoint that disconnects mid-request\nmakes three attempts and then fails; an unauthenticated fetch of a gated\nrepo stops after one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(release): hand dist/ back to the runner after the container build\n\nThe wheel build runs as root in the container while the steps around it\nrun as the runner user on the host. On the 2026-09-21 scheduled run\n(35568119321) 'Record what this wheel was built against' died writing\ndist/provenance-<flavor>.txt into the root-owned dist/ the build had just\ncreated: Permission denied, on both flavors, after the wheels themselves\nhad built and validated cleanly.\n\nchown dist/ back to the runner before leaving the build step. A chown\nrather than a pre-created directory, because a previous run on the same\nworkspace can leave a root-owned dist/ behind that checkout's clean does\nnot remove.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(release): refuse stale release refs; tag the release ref, not the branch head\n\nThe 2026-09-21 scheduled run (35568119321) derived v0.1.6, found the\nrelease/v0.1.6 branch an earlier failed run had left on July's\nv0.1.6-rc0, and tagged that stale head instead of main -- so the wheels\nit built (had the build not died on dist/ ownership) would have been\nJuly's code shipped as v0.1.6.\n\nThree changes to the resolve step:\n- a pre-existing release branch that is not where the release ref\n  resolves is now refused, with the cleanup spelled out, instead of\n  being silently built from\n- a newly created tag lands on the release ref's commit, not on the\n  branch head (identical when the branch was just created; the only\n  case where they differ is exactly the stale-branch case)\n- a pre-existing tag that is not where the release ref resolves is\n  refused the same way, because the build checks the tag out: a stale\n  tag ships stale code no matter where the branch points\n\naiter's release-automation.yaml carries the same tag-on-branch-head\nlogic this was modeled on.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: silence the automation's own tag push; catch a masked smoke failure; stop retrying permanent download failures\n\nThree review findings:\n\n- The resolve step pushed the release tag with the app token checkout\n  persisted, and a push made with an app installation token fires\n  \\`on: push: tags\\`: the 2026-09-22 dispatch started a second full\n  two-flavor build of the same release (run 35682961559). The prepare job\n  now rides GITHUB_TOKEN -- a push made with GITHUB_TOKEN triggers no\n  workflow events -- so creating the tag cannot fire this workflow again.\n  A tag a human pushes still releases; only the automation's own pushes\n  go silent.\n\n- The nightly smoke check ran \\`simple_inference | grep\\` inside bash -c\n  without pipefail, so the pipeline's status was grep's: an inference\n  that printed its prompts and completions and then died still read as\n  success, skipped the hub probe and passed the nightly on a failed\n  image. pipefail inside the exec makes the python exit status count.\n\n- The download retry treated every status but 2 and 124 as transport, so\n  a full filesystem, an unwritable staging directory or a broken import\n  was retried three times with sleeps before failing with the same\n  diagnosis. The python side now classifies: 2 a refusal, 3 transport\n  (httpx.TransportError, the backend huggingface_hub 1.x actually uses,\n  plus builtin connection/timeout errors and HTTP 408/429/5xx), 1\n  everything else -- local and permanent. Only 3 is retried.\n\nVerified with three new tests that run the shipped files verbatim: the\nretry classification against a stub hub (transport 3 attempts exit 3,\nENOSPC 1 attempt exit 1, gated 1 attempt exit 2, HTTP 503 3 attempts\nexit 3), the smoke command against a stub python3 that prints matching\nlines and then fails (caught with pipefail, passes without), and the\npush credential structurally (write permission, no token override, no\napp token, tag trigger kept). The resolve matrix (9/9), the dist\nownership test (2/2) and actionlint from the repo root are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: zufayu <zufayu@amd.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: zufayu <8138883+zufayu@users.noreply.github.com>",
