          "id": "514f21250c0e987a8dc699c1c3d2a3b6d11bca9d",
          "message": "ci: build LMCache ROCm torch 2.10 wheels from any commit (#2388)\n\n* ci: build LMCache ROCm torch 2.10 wheels from any commit\n\nATOM's image ships AMD's ROCm 7.2.4 / torch 2.10 build, but LMCache only\npublishes a wheel for that ABI with tagged releases. Its rolling\nnightly-rocm wheel targets torch 2.11 and fails to load here\n(undefined c10::cuda::CUDACachingAllocator symbol), so an LMCache fix on\ndev could not reach ATOM until the next tag.\n\nAdd a manually dispatched workflow that builds LMCache at a given commit\nwith LMCache's own build script inside the same digest-pinned\nrocm/pytorch 2.10 image LMCache uses, validates it in a clean container\n(LMCache's ABI validator plus an ATOM check for the MP adapters, native\nentry points and the MP server flags ATOM launches with), and optionally\npublishes it as an immutable pre-release that the Dockerfiles can pin.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci(tmp): run the LMCache wheel build on push to this branch\n\nTemporary, to exercise the build job on GitHub before merge; revert\nbefore merging.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Revert \"ci(tmp): run the LMCache wheel build on push to this branch\"\n\nThe build job passed on build-only-atom:\nhttps://github.com/ROCm/ATOM/actions/runs/35982738885\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Honglie Yi <hyi@crsuse2-m2m-v2-020.us-east2-a.compute.internal>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
